  "findings": [
    "Bulk completion bookkeeping is a measured hotspot: concrete BTreeMap<OperationId, oneshot::Sender<OperationId>>::insert/remove physical functions account for19.32% of observed CPU-delta weight. Frozen799f2cf actor source binds this map to per-original replies at lines38/242/329. This is matched host-adapter bookkeeping, not a production consensus-engine CPU share.",
    "Bulk _platform_memmove is7.53%, LogEntry::clone2.71%, SlicePartialEq<LogEntry>::equal_same_length1.03%. Native physical symbols identify these operations; they do not establish an allocator cause or prove all copies originate in one subsystem.",
    "Singleton71.0% and bulk33.3% of observed deltas are attached to a currently sampled __psynch_cvwait stack. CPU occurred earlier in the sampling interval, possibly during short task bursts. This is NOT CPU consumed while blocked and cannot identify a precise blocking instruction hotspot.",
    "Sidecar native-symbol resolution covers94.60%/97.22% of leaf CPU-delta weight. Inline/source chains are rendered, but0.13.1 coalesces them by native symbol start address, so individual inline line costs remain representative.",
    "Use these graphs to select further bounded measurements; they are not sustained unprofiled floor acceptance, leader/follower CPU attribution or additive inclusive CPU phases."
